{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DK4vPk1FgbMLpUvMPG9Vhw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Epic 04 Fix Batch 001 (from canonical epic-review 001, impl-lead curated)\n2\t\n3\tImpl-lead ruling on EV-04-001 (recorded here as the governing decision for item 1): RATIFY form-entry queue semantics. TC-4.1 requires the queue section to be consistent with the per-form state counts in the same report (queued+claimed = pending+retrying identity); counting work items would break that identity (one turn_derivation work item backs two form rows by design, turns/internal/forms.ts). The implementation stands; the spec wording is amended to match the ratified contract. Do not change health.ts queue-counting behavior.\n4\t\n5\t- [ ] EV-04-001 (ratification, docs only): Amend AC-4.5's wording in `epic.md` and tech-design Flow 4 (`tech-design.md`) to state the ratified contract explicitly: health.queue reports queued/claimed counts per form-report entry via live queue-item joins (so the queued+claimed = pending+retrying identity holds), not raw work-item counts from listQueuedWork; remove/replace the Flow 4 sentence naming listQueuedWork as a health input and the External Contracts row listing listQueuedWork as \"Used by ... health\". Add a short code comment at the queue-count site in `src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts` stating one work item may back multiple form entries and counts are per-entry by ratified contract (Epic 04 fix-batch-001).\n6\t- [ ] EV-04-002 (doc lag): Update `epic.md` lines ~149/156-157, `test-plan.md` line ~38, and `stories/coverage.md` line ~48 so \"byte-identical pull outputs and materialized files\" records the approved Story 4 ruling-011 contract: pull outputs literally byte-identical; materialized files byte-identical after normalizing only the thread id, ids asserted to differ.\n7\t- [ ] EV-04-002 (doc lag): Update tech-design DD-4 wording (~line 94) from stored-band-token sum to the approved Story 3 ruling-011 contract: loadCost.bandTokens measured from pull-served band messages; per-band stored token counts remain reported in the band section.\n8\t- [ ] EV-04-002 (doc lag): Update `stories/03-view-contents-report.md` Spec Deviations section from \"None.\" to record approved ruling-011 (measured bandTokens; nullable sourceState for never-compacted threads).\n9\t- [ ] Cleanup: remove the stale stub-era comment at `src/cli/index.ts:473-475` referring to the pre-Story-3 inspect.view stub.\n10\t\n11\tOut of scope (deliberately not in this batch): overview boundary sourced via pull.meta because ViewStatus exposes no boundaryPosition (non-blocking observation; future enhancement).\n12\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"48f0488f-987d-49fe-9ed6-d5d9068f93c3","uuid":"adbcb212-50a0-4785-ab11-2307e30e5cd4","timestamp":"2026-06-12T15:55:33.739Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/epic/fix-batch-001.md","content":"# Epic 04 Fix Batch 001 (from canonical epic-review 001, impl-lead curated)\n\nImpl-lead ruling on EV-04-001 (recorded here as the governing decision for item 1): RATIFY form-entry queue semantics. TC-4.1 requires the queue section to be consistent with the per-form state counts in the same report (queued+claimed = pending+retrying identity); counting work items would break that identity (one turn_derivation work item backs two form rows by design, turns/internal/forms.ts). The implementation stands; the spec wording is amended to match the ratified contract. Do not change health.ts queue-counting behavior.\n\n- [ ] EV-04-001 (ratification, docs only): Amend AC-4.5's wording in `epic.md` and tech-design Flow 4 (`tech-design.md`) to state the ratified contract explicitly: health.queue reports queued/claimed counts per form-report entry via live queue-item joins (so the queued+claimed = pending+retrying identity holds), not raw work-item counts from listQueuedWork; remove/replace the Flow 4 sentence naming listQueuedWork as a health input and the External Contracts row listing listQueuedWork as \"Used by ... health\". Add a short code comment at the queue-count site in `src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts` stating one work item may back multiple form entries and counts are per-entry by ratified contract (Epic 04 fix-batch-001).\n- [ ] EV-04-002 (doc lag): Update `epic.md` lines ~149/156-157, `test-plan.md` line ~38, and `stories/coverage.md` line ~48 so \"byte-identical pull outputs and materialized files\" records the approved Story 4 ruling-011 contract: pull outputs literally byte-identical; materialized files byte-identical after normalizing only the thread id, ids asserted to differ.\n- [ ] EV-04-002 (doc lag): Update tech-design DD-4 wording (~line 94) from stored-band-token sum to the approved Story 3 ruling-011 contract: loadCost.bandTokens measured from pull-served band messages; per-band stored token counts remain reported in the band section.\n- [ ] EV-04-002 (doc lag): Update `stories/03-view-contents-report.md` Spec Deviations section from \"None.\" to record approved ruling-011 (measured bandTokens; nullable sourceState for never-compacted threads).\n- [ ] Cleanup: remove the stale stub-era comment at `src/cli/index.ts:473-475` referring to the pre-Story-3 inspect.view stub.\n\nOut of scope (deliberately not in this batch): overview boundary sourced via pull.meta because ViewStatus exposes no boundaryPosition (non-blocking observation; future enhancement).\n","numLines":12,"startLine":1,"totalLines":12}}}
