n\":\"accept-threadId-normalized-materialized-file-equality-and-update-story-spec\",\"rationale\":\"AC-5.3's intent is end-to-end determinism of derived content. The thread id is the design's one intentionally random value (threads design decision 7), so a fresh-thread replay can never be literally byte-identical without adding a test-only id-injection seam into production thread creation — exactly the non-designed shim the anti-shim rules prohibit. Normalizing only the thread id, asserting the two ids actually differ, and requiring every other byte exact is the strongest determinism proof available without weakening production. Pull-output hash equality (which contains no thread id) remains literal. Approved as the accepted contract for TC-5.2/TC-5.3.\",\"source\":\"impl-lead (Claude Code caller harness)\"}]},\"runtimeIdentity\":{\"version\":\"0.4.0\",\"invocationSource\":\"unknown\",\"entryPath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/lspec-core/dist/bin/lbuild-impl.js\"},\"replayBoundary\":{\"smallestSafeStep\":\"resume-from-last-valid-artifact\",\"reasoning\":\"Provider output became invalid after durable artifacts were written, so replay should resume from the last valid artifact boundary.\",\"validArtifactPaths\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/04-lifecycle-exercise/001-story-validate.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/04-lifecycle-exercise/003-implementor.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/04-lifecycle-exercise/004-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/04-lifecycle-exercise/story-lead/001-final-package.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/04-lifecycle-exercise/story-lead/001-ruling-response-00